WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Sikh scripture names the
divine with a numeral: one.

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.070
Its hymns often speak in a woman's voice,

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.650
as a bride longing for the Beloved.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.880
Yet most of those who have translated
and explained it have been men.

5
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:18.590
So is the scripture itself feminist, or
has Sikh history been retold to make it

6
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.080
look that way?

7
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.900
In this mission, you'll
compare two scholars,

8
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.940
Nikky-Guninder Kaur
Singh and Doris Jakobsh,

9
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.790
who answer this differently.

10
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.970
Then you'll test their ideas against
women's campaigns in Sikh communities today.

11
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.490
Your mission: weigh up two scholars'
readings of gender in Sikhism.
